---
layout: changelog
title: "Deploy Sites and Functions from Cursor Origin repositories"
date: 2026-11-27
cover: /images/blog/announcing-cursor-origin-support/cover.avif
tags: sites, functions, integrations
---

Origin, Cursor's Git hosting platform, is now one of Appwrite's Git providers. Connect a Cursor workspace from **Project settings** > **Git configuration** > **Add installation**, approve the installation on Cursor, and [deploy from Git](/docs/products/sites/deploy-from-git) on every push.

Pushes to your production branch build and activate. Pushes to other branches build without activating, and Sites get a private [preview link](/docs/products/sites/previews). Each build reports back to its commit as a check run, and pull requests get a build summary comment. Create repositories in Cursor first, since Origin doesn't let apps create them. Origin is available as a Git provider on Appwrite Cloud.

